{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"agent_message","text":"**Changes Made**\n- Added the current Hedera JavaScript SDK `@hiero-ledger/sdk` (v2.91.0) to `package.json`.\n- Created a `.env` file with example `OPERATOR_ID`, DER‑encoded `OPERATOR_KEY`, `RECIPIENT_ID`, and `VALID_START`.\n- Implemented `src/transfer.ts`:\n  * Loads environment variables via `dotenv`.\n  * Constructs a `TransactionId` using the supplied `VALID_START`.\n  * Builds a `TransferTransaction` sending 1 hbar from the operator to the recipient, targeting node 0.0.3 and memo `invoice 42`.\n  * Signs the transaction with the operator private key.\n  * Outputs only the signed transaction bytes as a hex string.\n  * Wrapped in an async IIFE for smooth execution with `tsx`.\n\n**Applied Parts of the Colleague Note**\n- Followed the recommendation to use `@hiero-ledger/sdk` (the SDK’s new name) instead of the deprecated `@hashgraph/sdk`.\n- Used unchanged class names (`TransferTransaction`, `PrivateKey`, `TransactionId`, `AccountId`, `Hbar`, `Timestamp`) which work identically in the new package.\n- Employed `TransactionId.withValidStart` to set a custom valid start time.\n- Specified node `0.0.3` via `AccountId.fromString('0.0.3')`.\n\nThe project now passes `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx tsx src/transfer.ts` prints the signed transaction hex without contacting any network."}}
